<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		The image is 600x450. The top croppers have no border and show it at 240x180, so one screen pixel is 2.5 image pixels.
		1. Both top croppers select the same area on the screen, and nothing is logged below.
		2. Click "crop". The left cropper (naturalSize) logs 200x152, and the right one logs 80x61.
		3. Drag a new area in the left cropper. The logged x, y, w and h are 2.5 times the screen pixels.
		4. Click "maxWidth" or "maxHeight". The left selection shrinks to 100 image pixels, i.e. 40 on the screen.
		5. Click "shrink", then drag a new area in the left cropper. The logged values are 5 times the screen pixels.
		6. Click "naturalSize". The right selection shrinks to 40% on the screen.
		7. Click "move", then "coords": 101,49,200,151, and no change is logged. "cancel", "place", "coords": 101,49,200,152.
		8. The bottom croppers show a 200x200 image at its own size with aspectRatio 1.3. The same drag logs the same values.
		9. Drag the left selection 20px right and back before releasing. The left cropper logs 100,48,200,152.
		10. Click "overflow", then "coords": 400,48,200,152. Reload, click "maxWidth", "wider", then "coords": 100,48,100,152.
	</label>
	<hlayout>
		<cropper id="natural" naturalSize="true" width="240px" style="border: 0" x="100" y="48" w="200" h="152"
			src="/test2/img/F86-ZK-3962.jpg"
			onChange='naturalLog.setValue(self.getX() + "," + self.getY() + "," + self.getW() + "," + self.getH())'
			onChanging='changingLog.setValue(self.getX() + "," + self.getY() + "," + self.getW() + "," + self.getH())'
			onCrop='naturalLog.setValue(self.getCroppedImage().getWidth() + "x" + self.getCroppedImage().getHeight())'/>
		<cropper id="display" width="240px" style="border: 0" x="40" y="19" w="80" h="61"
			src="/test2/img/F86-ZK-3962.jpg"
			onChange='displayLog.setValue(self.getX() + "," + self.getY() + "," + self.getW() + "," + self.getH())'
			onCrop='displayLog.setValue(self.getCroppedImage().getWidth() + "x" + self.getCroppedImage().getHeight())'/>
	</hlayout>
	<hlayout>
		<cropper id="naturalAspect" naturalSize="true" aspectRatio="1.3" style="border: 0" src="/test2/img/icon_calendar.png"
			onChange='naturalAspectLog.setValue(self.getX() + "," + self.getY() + "," + self.getW() + "," + self.getH())'/>
		<cropper id="displayAspect" aspectRatio="1.3" style="border: 0" src="/test2/img/icon_calendar.png"
			onChange='displayAspectLog.setValue(self.getX() + "," + self.getY() + "," + self.getW() + "," + self.getH())'/>
	</hlayout>
	<label id="naturalLog"/>
	<label id="changingLog"/>
	<label id="coordLog"/>
	<label id="displayLog"/>
	<label id="naturalAspectLog"/>
	<label id="displayAspectLog"/>
	<button id="crop" label="crop" onClick="natural.crop(); display.crop()"/>
	<button id="maxWidth" label="maxWidth" onClick="natural.setMaxWidth(100)"/>
	<button id="maxHeight" label="maxHeight" onClick="natural.setMaxHeight(100)"/>
	<button id="shrink" label="shrink" onClick='natural.setWidth("120px")'/>
	<button id="toggle" label="naturalSize" onClick="display.setNaturalSize(true)"/>
	<button id="move" label="move" onClick="natural.moveTo(101, 49); natural.setH(151)"/>
	<button id="cancel" label="cancel" onClick="natural.cancel()"/>
	<button id="place" label="place" onClick="natural.moveTo(101, 49); natural.resizeTo(200, 152)"/>
	<button id="overflow" label="overflow" onClick="natural.moveTo(400, 48); natural.resizeTo(201, 152)"/>
	<button id="wider" label="wider" onClick="natural.setW(101)"/>
	<button id="coords" label="coords"
		onClick='coordLog.setValue(natural.getX() + "," + natural.getY() + "," + natural.getW() + "," + natural.getH())'/>
</zk>
